From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: render external taskbar native ReBar grippers

Native XP taskbar ReBar closes its initial generic theme on SetWindowTheme
but paints a classic gripper afterward. Keep its native window procedure,
input, band layout and dragging. Only under external-shell opt-in and the
Taskbar app theme, overlay hidden-title band headers with the actual themed
parent background and Taskbar::Rebar gripper at public RB_GETRECT and
RB_GETBANDINFOW geometry. Use the real theme part size, preserve print DC
state and clipping, and safely handle destruction during native paint.
No Microsoft code or resource data is embedded.

The public rebar-theme regression compares the output against direct active
theme rendering, checks translated print DCs, native input and paint results,
disabling the override, and destruction from the original paint procedure.

